architecture account-workspace-mcp
  canonical_name AccountWorkspaceMcp
  source_path scripts/tests/installed-workspace-contract.test.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/fixtures/installed-workspace-contract.json
  witness scripts/tests/installed-workspace-contract.test.mjs imports exact retained store clients from eleven installed workspace packages across ten families and exercises native creation, edits, conflicts, tombstones, explicit restoration, atomic batches, lost-response readback, cross-account and revoked-write refusal in an isolated estate
  witness scripts/tests/installed-workspace-contract.test.mjs verifies Catalogue and Room Planning share one destination-owned object and attachment through their original family binding
  forbidden_inference shared storage-contract acceptance -> complete domain editors, archived-product UX, historical revision browsing, cross-family object identity or a live customer write
  family surface
  domain Account / Product continuity through MCP
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can a signed-in assistant read and revise the same private draft that its user opens in an installed product, without copying records or widening account access?
  purpose Project existing installed workspace bindings, revisioned drafts and compatible editor continuations through the account MCP carrier, with scalar changes and domain-validated workbook reviews delegated to existing product and native storage owners.
  source_path integrations/mcp/workspace_mcp.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/workbook_mcp.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/workbook_app_resource.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-controller.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-app.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-app.html
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-build.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/application_continuation.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/application_views.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/workspace_records.h
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/workspace_mcp.test.mjs exercises real Auth, CMS, WebAddress and OAuth calls across catalogue, room, audio and recurring-program draft families, exact previews, cross-editor continuation, concurrent edits, current role revocation and lost-response reconciliation
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh retains the separate delegated institution aperture and full administrator boundary
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp.test.mjs verifies gateway discovery, bounded workbook reads, source-address inspection, exact previews, Univer edits, shared review decisions, native permission checks, concurrency bounds and lost-response reconciliation
  invariant the request carries its own authenticated session to a deployment-fixed workspace owner; caller arguments cannot select an actor, namespace, database, credential or endpoint
  invariant the machine binding directory projects the same query and permission checks as Your work; unavailable or incomplete listings refuse rather than manufacturing an empty success
  invariant workspace_records retains whole-body SHA-256, revision and immutable file references without hydrating media or copying records into another store
  invariant generic scalar previews bind the exact binding, key, source digest, expected revision and encoded candidate; workspace_update preserves record structure and file references
  invariant workbook tools fetch bounded workbook and decision bodies, and baseline cells only when requested; they do not download original XLSX bytes
  invariant workbook previews run the existing Univer and review rules without writing files or records; commits recompute the same candidate with a fifteen-minute review time and retain unchanged original source references
  invariant at most two workbook operations run concurrently per account carrier instance; worker calculation has a termination deadline and model-visible reads have page and output bounds
  invariant native WebAddress rechecks current destination access and CMS commits against the expected revision and existing request ledger; transport failures do not trigger automatic write retries
  invariant native continuation links preserve destination, compatible editor release and saved record identity; unrelated product families are not joined merely because one account can open both
  invariant declared collection links use retained CONTINUATIONS profiles, including exact-key profiles within a family; record families without a compatible view keep their visible prefix and open the verified owning editor
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/installed_subtools_test.mjs checks mapped collections, exact-key audio imports, supporting incoming records and current destination refusal without creating record views
  invariant delegated private-product sessions retain their existing restricted tool slice; the account workspace carrier is exposed in personal and Bonfyre administrator apertures
  known_gap generic scalar editing does not run each product domain compiler; only the explicit workbook tools invoke the financial workbook validation and calculation owner
  known_gap workbook tools require the ServiceSite Univer dependencies in the gateway deployment; current tests do not establish live availability
  invariant embedded financial views use the official MCP Apps SDK and the same account tools; the static UI resource contains no workbook data or credentials
  invariant a preview is consumed before dispatch; interrupted saves require a successful record reload, and host notifications cannot replace unfinished edits or confirmed changes
  known_gap the financial MCP App has protocol and native-owner tests; actual host rendering, browser interaction, public demo adoption, collaborative cursors, cross-destination transfers and provider effects remain unverified
  forbidden_inference a saved draft or matching preview -> a valid commercial agreement, order, publication, payment, authority grant or performed work
  forbidden_inference fixture coverage of four draft families -> all products are integrated or a live deployment has been verified
  interacts account-mcp-continues-native-workspace
  interacts account-mcp-operates-financial-workbook
  interacts account-mcp-embeds-financial-review

interaction account-mcp-continues-native-workspace
  source account-workspace-mcp
  destination web-address-edge
  relation current-session-private-product-continuation
  preserves current account session, destination and role checks, installed application binding, exact record identity, source revision and digest, immutable media references, native write receipt and compatible editor links
  drops model-generated authority claims, arbitrary endpoints and identities, copied record stores, original media downloads, automatic retries and inferred external effects
  forbidden_inference successful MCP transport -> authority beyond the native destination or a completed product operation
  invalidates_on session revocation, destination grants, installation state, native record revisions, editor release or workspace transport contract changes
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/workspace_mcp.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/workspace_mcp.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/application_continuation.h

interaction account-mcp-operates-financial-workbook
  source account-workspace-mcp
  destination financial-workbook
  relation shared-workbook-calculation-and-review
  preserves exact saved record revision and digest, original source references, mapped transaction fields, actual Univer edits and recalculation, content-bound row decisions and native current access checks
  drops scalar patches to workbook blobs, inferred recalculation from cached values, implicit source lineage after moved rows and independent financial approval claims
  forbidden_inference a workbook tool save -> ledger posting, reconciled accounts, verified financial advice, live deployment or an embedded MCP App
  invalidates_on workbook schema, review fingerprint semantics, supported formulas, native blob transport, session grants or gateway runtime dependencies changing
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/workbook_mcp.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-review.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-calculation.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-calculation-worker.mjs

interaction account-mcp-embeds-financial-review
  source account-workspace-mcp
  destination financial-workbook
  relation embedded-review-over-existing-account-tools
  preserves current account authorization, workbook identity and revision, bounded source comparison, explicit change confirmation, interrupted-save request identity and exact native editor continuation
  drops independent UI credentials, a second record store, host notifications replacing unfinished work, implicit write retries and claims of verified browser rendering
  forbidden_inference SDK handshake or native integration tests -> usable rendering in any particular MCP host, accessibility, financial approval or live deployment
  invalidates_on MCP Apps SDK contract, workbook tool responses, gateway resource routing, static bundle, installed release or native permissions changing
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp.test.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp-controller.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh
  binding integrations/mcp/workbook_app_resource.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-app.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-controller.mjs
